/ Named values belong to their type (ruling 3). separator becomes a text — it goes under
/ text, with its named values ("line", "comma", "tab", "space", "semicolon") held as its
/ own list. The proof stage 2 names: `%line% is text` is true (red today — separator is
/ its own top-level type today, deriving from item, not text).
NamedValuesBelongToTheType
- variable.set(Name=%line%, Value="line", Type={name:"separator"})
- condition.if(Left=%line%, Operator="is", Right="text") { variable.set(Name=%isText%, Value=true) }
- assert.equals(Expected=true, Actual=%isText%, Message="a separator is a text")
